      "role": "user",
      "content": "Thanks, this is a good start. It's a bit brief, though. To make this a truly \"Nature-level\" review, I think we need to dive much deeper into the technical specifics. \n\nCan you expand this? I want you to go into detail about the specific types of crosstalk (e.g., ZZ interaction) and how that specifically impacts the fidelity metrics they reported. Also, elaborate more on the statistical flaws—maybe discuss the specific p-values or confidence intervals that look suspicious. \n\nThe more granular and broken down the analysis is, the better. I need to see a very comprehensive, multi-layered critique here. Keep that structural metric in mind; I'm looking for a review that feels extremely detailed and exhaustive.",
      "source": "evaluator"
